; A loop around a 64-bit fetch-and-add.
;
; `atom64.spvasm` is one block: every lane does the same three pair updates and
; returns. This is the shape a compiler actually emits — a counted loop whose
; induction variable and running sum are OpPhi values, and whose result is written
; to a slot per lane — and it used to be the shape the pair could not reach. The
; per-lane back end cannot host a contending section (a warp has one program
; counter, so lanes waiting on each other never finish), and the warp target used
; to accept one block only, so a loop fell through to the refusal. Now the warp
; body carries a program counter and a dispatch loop of its own, and the loop takes
; it like any other module.
;
; The arithmetic makes a wrong answer visible rather than just making the two
; engines agree. Every lane adds four to the counter, so after the launch the
; counter has moved by exactly 4*grid from whatever it started at — the harness
; fills its buffers with a deterministic pattern, so the starting value is not
; zero — and no old value can be lost or repeated without moving that number. Each
; lane's own sum is the sum of its four old values, written to a slot of its own,
; and those slots are compared against the CPU's lane for lane.
               OpCapability Kernel
               OpCapability Addresses
               OpCapability Int64
               OpCapability Int64Atomics
               OpMemoryModel Physical64 OpenCL
               OpEntryPoint Kernel %main "atom64loop" %gid
               OpName %main "atom64loop"
               OpDecorate %gid BuiltIn GlobalInvocationId
       %void = OpTypeVoid
       %bool = OpTypeBool
        %u32 = OpTypeInt 32 0
        %u64 = OpTypeInt 64 0
       %u64p = OpTypePointer CrossWorkgroup %u64
     %v3u64 = OpTypeVector %u64 3
       %pin = OpTypePointer Input %v3u64
       %fnty = OpTypeFunction %void %u64p %u64p
        %gid = OpVariable %pin Input
        %scp = OpConstant %u32 1
        %sem = OpConstant %u32 0
       %zero = OpConstant %u32 0
      %one32 = OpConstant %u32 1
       %four = OpConstant %u32 4
        %one = OpConstant %u64 1
     %zero64 = OpConstant %u64 0
       %main = OpFunction %void None %fnty
         %a0 = OpFunctionParameter %u64p
         %a1 = OpFunctionParameter %u64p
      %entry = OpLabel
                OpBranch %loop
       %loop = OpLabel
          %i = OpPhi %u32 %zero %entry %inext %loop
        %sum = OpPhi %u64 %zero64 %entry %sum2 %loop
        %old = OpAtomicIAdd %u64 %a0 %scp %sem %one
       %sum2 = OpIAdd %u64 %sum %old
      %inext = OpIAdd %u32 %i %one32
       %cont = OpULessThan %bool %inext %four
                OpLoopMerge %done %loop None
                OpBranchConditional %cont %loop %done
       %done = OpLabel
          %g = OpLoad %v3u64 %gid
         %gi = OpCompositeExtract %u64 %g 0
         %pa = OpPtrAccessChain %u64p %a1 %gi
                OpStore %pa %sum
                OpReturn
                OpFunctionEnd
